1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,780
What should I do?

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:05,900
What should I do?

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:10,220
After three losses, your status as a selector is revoked.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:13,280
As for your wish, it becomes corrupted.

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,920
All I can tell you is her wish was to make friends.

6
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,240
You can imagine what a corruption of that would be.

7
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,700
So you're saying she lost her friends?

8
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:26,460
Far worse than that.

9
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,320
She can never make friends again.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,300
Horrible, but unfortunately there's more.

11
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,900
With her third loss, not only is her selector status gone...

12
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,260
Hitoi can't read it anymore.

13
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:40,100
She said that all the words were disappearing.

14
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,900
She also tells me she doesn't remember you.

15
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:48,120
So are all her memories related to those battles, as if they never even took place.

16
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,700
There has to be something I can do.

17
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:53,980
Anything!

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,260
Please be there.

19
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:08,680
Kuribayashi residence.

20
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,240
Oh, Ruko.

21
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,620
How are you doing?

22
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:13,660
I heard you were sick.

23
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:16,900
Um, hey, is Yuzuki home?

24
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,140
No, she's still out.

25
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:21,980
What's wrong?

26
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,000
Are you okay?

27
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,600
Uh, yep, just Peachy.

28
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:26,560
See ya!

29
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,380
Ruko?

30
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:28,880
Bro?

31
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:08,380
めくりめくる楽 目まぐるしいステージで

32
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:19,380
その絡まった感情 満足いくまで何回も壊してしまえ

33
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:24,380
運命に手招きされ彷徨う明日は

34
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:30,380
何を選んで何を手放し 一つになればいいんだろう

35
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:35,380
なじった毒がおさらす余裕なんてないよ

36
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:40,380
乾いた後悔の海を飲み干す君は

37
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:46,380
限られた言葉でいつしかの笑顔 許して欲しいんだろう

38
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:51,380
現実を忘れたって 構わないよ

39
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:56,380
だから 今も知らないでいたいな

40
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:04,380
ご視聴ありがとうございました

41
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,380
1,2,1,2

42
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:22,380
2,1,2、メイマイラしていない

43
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:33,380
1,2,1、2,1、2、2、1、3、5、1、2、1、3、8、1 まず

44
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,220
Yuzuki?

45
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:37,260
No, I haven't seen her today.

46
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,500
Why, is something up?

47
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,340
No!

48
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,420
I summon Amber, and I attack you with it!

49
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,420
Ugh!

50
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,420
Man, if only I pulled guard!

51
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:47,960
At least tell me what's wrong!

52
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:04,380
Woo!

53
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:17,800
Hey, if you're sad, tell me why.

54
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:20,620
I know!

55
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:21,760
Let's battle!

56
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,540
A battle will make you happy again!

57
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,220
You'll see.

58
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:28,180
You just wanted to see me suffer, didn't you?

59
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:30,300
And I bet you enjoyed it!

60
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:32,500
You're wrong, that's not true!

61
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,500
It's not true!

62
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,500
So why can't I stop?

63
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:54,500
Crud, that way's blocked.

64
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:11,500
Is there another way to reach Akira? I'm having no luck.

65
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,500
Big surprise. What do you need her for?

66
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:19,500
Well, because she took some outfits home last time.

67
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:21,500
Are you nuts? Why'd you let her do that?

68
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:26,500
I'm sorry. She swore she was gonna bring them back, but then we canned her.

69
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,500
Terrific.

70
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,500
Why can't they get in touch with Akira?

71
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,500
Hey, who are you?

72
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,500
Um, I'm a...

73
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:37,500
You here for a shoot? For which magazine?

74
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:41,500
Well, it's... or um... it's... it's called...

75
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Oh, there you are.

76
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,500
Huh?

77
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:47,500
It's okay. She's my guest here tonight.

78
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:51,500
Oh, she is? Oh geez, no one warned me. Sorry, Iona.

79
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,500
Iona...

80
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,500
Look, I...

81
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:17,500
You came here because you wanted to battle. Can't fight the urge anymore, can you?

82
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:21,500
No! You're wrong! I just wanted to see Akira and talk to her about...

83
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,500
That loser? What do you want with her?

84
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:24,500
Just to talk.

85
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:30,500
Well, you're too late. She's not here anymore. In fact, I highly doubt we'll ever be seeing her again.

86
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,500
Why?

87
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:35,500
She lost a battle to us. She lost one to you too, right?

88
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,500
You came here to see what happened to her, didn't you? Make sure she was okay?

89
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:46,500
Oh, that's so sweet. Then again, maybe you just came here to rub your victory in her stupid face.

90
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,500
That's not funny, okay?

91
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:54,500
Oh, chill. And by the way, Akira lost to another selector besides you two.

92
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,500
Wait, then that means...

93
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:02,500
Yep, that makes three losses. So game over, goodbye, and good riddance to bad rubbish.

94
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:09,500
I... I didn't know. Where is she? Is she okay?

95
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:16,500
Who cares? But if I had to guess, she's probably crying her eyes out somewhere. Just like your other loser friend did.

96
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,500
What other friend?

97
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:20,500
The mousy little wallflower with the glasses.

98
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:23,500
Hichoe? Oh God, what did you do to her?

99
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,500
Same as we did to Akira.

100
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:26,500
Gave her a beating.

101
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:40,500
A battle? With me?

102
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:47,500
Sorry. But Hichoe's wish has already come true. She doesn't need to battle. Thank you both. But no.

103
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:57,500
Well, if she's already had her wish fulfilled, what does she have to lose? Come on, just one match.

104
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:06,500
I'm sure you know how important a wish can be. Iona's really giving it her all to have hers come true. It'd mean so much if you helped her out.

105
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:13,500
She has a point. I already made friends, so no matter how this match goes down, I'm still a winner.

106
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:16,500
Hichoe...

107
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:20,500
Alright then, I'll battle you.

108
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:25,500
Lucky for us, your little four-eyed friend didn't know what would happen if she lost three times.

109
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:31,500
Wait, you... you knew Hichoe already had two losses but still did it? How could you?

110
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:36,500
You monsters, that's horrible!

111
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,500
Want to battle us for revenge?

112
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:42,500
We hurt one of your friends, so I'm sure you want to even the score.

113
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:45,500
You won't get a better chance than this.

114
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,500
Let's battle!

115
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:53,500
Even if I did, it won't help Hichoe... or her wish.

116
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:58,500
And yours?

117
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,500
What?

118
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:03,500
Your wish. Did you find one?

119
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,500
Well, I...

120
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,500
Aha, so you did.

121
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:08,500
No, I still don't have one.

122
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,500
Liar.

123
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,500
You know, I remember what you said to me.

124
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:17,500
That a selector battling without a wish was blasphemy, whatever that means.

125
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:22,500
Well, it's a good thing I don't have one, because either way, I'll never battle again.

126
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:28,500
No! Please don't give up, Ru! I love battling with you more than anything! Don't quit now!

127
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:33,500
Tom, I... sorry. But I'm done. No more.

128
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:40,500
Tell me, Little Miss Drama Queen. Wanting friends? Being with someone you love? Those are both pretty lame wishes, don't you think?

129
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,500
No! Not at all!

130
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:45,500
Deep down, you agree, because your wish is a lot more exciting.

131
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,500
I told you, I don't have a wish!

132
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:51,500
You do. Don't try to hide it, because we know.

133
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:55,500
How can you tell me that when I don't even know? Why are you saying this stuff?

134
00:09:55,500 --> 00:10:08,500
Because you and I have the same wish. It's that feeling. I love it too.

135
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:14,500
My life wasn't bad before I started playing, but it wasn't especially good either.

136
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:17,500
Wh-what do you mean?

137
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:27,500
I never gave my life much thought. Just accepted it for what it was. Until I found her. And then, that's when I first felt it.

138
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:52,500
I understood it. I savored that feeling. It gave me purpose. It made me feel truly alive for the very first time. It felt like destiny. Like it was part of my soul. Doing battle is in my blood. In my flesh. In my bones. Do you see? It is my very being.

139
00:10:52,500 --> 00:11:03,500
But, come on. If you lose three times, you suffer a terrible fate. And even if you win, someone else will suffer instead. How is that good?

140
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:13,500
Perhaps it's not. But it is the nature of battle. And our nature as well. Both mine, and yours.

141
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:15,500
Is she wrong?

142
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,500
Stop it. Please just don't…

143
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:24,500
Why not be honest with yourself? I know you've felt it. And once you have, there's no way you can ever quit.

144
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:32,500
Say what you like, but you still yearn for it. You lust for battle. For victory.

145
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:39,500
I want nothing more than to battle you. And you me?

146
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:54,500
I do. Yay! Yes, I'd like to battle you. I really would. Badly. But you see…

147
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,500
Open!

148
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,500
Open!

149
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:18,500
What's the matter? We both heard you. You said you wanted to battle.

150
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,500
But that's not what I meant!

151
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,500
You didn't let me finish!

152
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,500
Sorry, was there something else?

153
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,500
Who cares? Forget it and have some fun!

154
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,500
Good. Now let's do this thing.

155
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,500
Battle!

156
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,500
Battle!

157
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,500
Hey, Will!

158
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,500
This is just sad.

159
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,500
Even your pal Hitoi put up more of a fight

160
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,500
and you know how pathetic she is.

161
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,500
A spell to search for low-level cards?

162
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,500
Why would she use that now?

163
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,500
I don't get it.

164
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,500
Something's not right here.

165
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:49,500
Why is she only using low-level attacks?

166
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:51,500
Time to grow!

167
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:55,500
Wake up, Gru!

168
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,500
It's time to get serious!

169
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,500
Nice move, Yona.

170
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:03,500
Yona!

171
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:04,500
Wake up, Gru!

172
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,500
It's time to get serious!

173
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,500
Nice move, Yona.

174
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:19,500
If you could see what cards were missing from your deck, you could find out which ones were used for your life cloth.

175
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,500
As a result, if Ruko attacks now...

176
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,500
As a result, if Ruko attacks now...

177
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,500
Tama, don't attack! Just end the turn early!

178
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,500
What?

179
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:30,500
Oh, too bad.

180
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,500
Your move!

181
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,500
Spell, blessed reminiscence!

182
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:34,500
I knew it!

183
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:35,500
Alright!

184
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,500
Arch-ambi spell!

185
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,500
Yeah!

186
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,500
Woo!

187
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:57,500
Well played, Tama!

188
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:59,500
Well played, Tama!

189
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:00,500
I knew it!

190
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:01,500
I knew it!

191
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,500
I knew it!

192
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,500
I knew it!

193
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,500
I knew it!

194
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:11,500
So, how long can you keep fighting like this?

195
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,500
Long as it takes!

196
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,500
Forever!

197
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,500
Forever?

198
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,500
I don't know what that word means!

199
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,500
It means for all time!

200
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,500
Oh, it does?

201
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,500
Then yes!

202
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,500
Of course!

203
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,500
I want to battle forever!

204
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:24,500
It's a word!

205
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,500
How about you?

206
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,500
Yuzuki...

207
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:39,500
Over there...

208
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,500
A selector...

209
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,500
Uh...

210
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,500
Huh?

211
00:15:53,500 --> 00:16:05,500
It's her.

212
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:08,420
Where's Iona?

213
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,760
The dressing room, I guess.

214
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,380
Well, instead of guessing, go find her and bring her in here.

215
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,140
Yes, sir. Right away, sir.

216
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:24,240
Yes. She's definitely the one.

217
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:29,440
Hey, Iona. What the...

218
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:42,400
Finally. I found her.

219
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:45,080
Tama! Wish crisis attack!

220
00:16:46,140 --> 00:17:05,320
At last.

221
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:17,520
There you are. They're waiting for you in Studio A. They need you there as soon as possible.

222
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,420
Okay. I'll be right there.

223
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:24,520
That was incredible.

224
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:28,760
Please tell me you agree.

225
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:32,600
Uh, well, I, um, maybe, but...

226
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:35,560
It was great! It's the most fun in the whole world!

227
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:38,580
I can't wait for the next one! I want to battle these guys forever!

228
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,680
I think quitting was a bad idea. We should do this more!

229
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,420
And you think so too, right, Ru?

230
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:45,420
Well, what do you say?

231
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,420
You're the one.

232
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:52,680
No.

233
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,600
We won.

234
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:08,440
Yeah.

235
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:10,300
Wonder how many losses she has now.

236
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:10,760
Ah...

237
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:27,040
No, I'll go.

238
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:29,600
But you stay here in case she comes back.

239
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:30,480
All right.

240
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:33,380
So this cafe you were saying Ruko went to

241
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:35,360
with her friend's mom, it's just down the street?

242
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:36,580
Yes, dear.

243
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,940
She said they were talking and all of a sudden

244
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:40,900
Rue got upset and just ran out of there.

245
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,140
Weird. Don't know what that's about.

246
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:45,280
Well, you can ask her later,

247
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:46,920
because I'm sure Rue's just fine.

248
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:55,780
What happened back there?

249
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,040
How could I?

250
00:18:58,420 --> 00:18:59,760
I gave in to temptation.

251
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:01,120
I forgot about my friends.

252
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:03,060
Forgot about what I did to Akira.

253
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:05,400
Nothing else mattered.

254
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:06,840
That was incredible.

255
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,820
Please tell me you agree.

256
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:14,240
No, I wouldn't.

